WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 3: Fun and Games.

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.400
In this unit you will learn the words for games and play.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.960
They are words like bounce, roll, throw and catch.

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.280
You will name the parts of your body.

5
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.740
You will learn the words that say where a
thing is: on, under, next to, left and right.

6
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.500
You will play simple games.

7
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.100
You will try a game from another country.

8
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.300
You will listen to a funny story.

9
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.880
You will hear the short 'u' sound in sun, fun and duck.

10
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.540
Learn by playing.

11
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.360
That is the best way.

12
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.720
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:44.440
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
act out ball actions (bounce, roll, throw, catch, hit).

14
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.300
You will also name parts of the body
(hand, foot, ear, nose, shoulder, head…)

15
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:55.240
You will also say where something is (on,
under, next to) and show left and right.

16
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.020
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

17
00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:04.200
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: big, pig, six, dig, hit, bit.

18
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.220
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

19
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.440
The reading sequence includes Amal and
the Big Ball and Talk about Fun and Games.

20
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.900
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

21
00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.700
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

22
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.360
The first language focus is Tell what you can do at play.

23
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.200
Choose a game action you are good at.

24
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.160
Say the sentence, then show it with your body.

25
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.340
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

26
00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.600
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

27
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.680
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

28
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:53.540
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

29
00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.320
You are ready to begin.

30
00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:01.400
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

31
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.800
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
